SOAPBOX: This was my first solid attempt at an RTTY contest. Unfortunately, I was quickly disappointed when the rate—despite running High Power (around 500W)—dropped to as low as 15 QSOs per hour while I was trying to work additional contacts on VFO2. Sadly, I miscalculated and couldn't manage to last the full 46 hours of the contest. I struggled to wake up to my alarm, so 25-minute naps seemed to work best. Regardless, it was still a good result for my first time in this type of competition. I really don't like having to compete in the "Youth" overlay category against stations with far greater capabilities than some of the contest stations in my own country :( The 2BSIQ technique requires a station capable of SO2R with good filters, and at High Power levels, those filters are very expensive.
